Mumon wrote:
> Why does everything nethack related have to be sent out as source code
> instead of binaries.

Because it's easy to create binaries out of source code but not the
other way around and because binaries are platform dependant. I'm almost
certain that ttyplay was programmed with an unix audience in mind, so if
there were binaries, they'd most probably be unix binaries which
wouldn't run on Windows at all (nor on MacOS or unsupported unices). So
I think publishing source code that can be compiled on almost every
platform is the better solution.

